#. type: Title ===
#: cli.adoc:1664
#, no-wrap
msgid "PCB SVG export"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:1667
msgid "The `pcb export svg` command exports a board design to an SVG file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:1669
msgid ""
"Usage: `kicad-cli pcb export svg [--help] [--output OUTPUT_DIR] [--layers "
"LAYER_LIST] [--drawing-sheet SHEET_PATH] [--define-var KEY=VALUE] [--"
"subtract-soldermask] [--mirror] [--theme THEME_NAME] [--negative] [--black-"
"and-white] [--sketch-pads-on-fab-layers] [--hide-DNP-footprints-on-fab-"
"layers] [--sketch-DNP-footprints-on-fab-layers] [--crossout-DNP-footprints-"
"on-fab-layers] [--page-size-mode MODE] [--fit-page-to-board] [--exclude-"
"drawing-sheet] [--drill-shape-opt SHAPE_OPTION] [--common-layers "
"COMMON_LAYER_LIST] [--mode-single] [--mode-multi] [--plot-invisible-text] [--"
"scale SCALE] [--check-zones] INPUT_FILE`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: cli.adoc:1755
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `-h`, `--help`\n"
"    | Show help for the SVG file export command.\n"
"| `-o <output dir>`, `--output <output dir>`\n"
"    | The output folder or filename for the exported files. When `--mode-single`\n"
"      is used, this is the output filename. If `--output` is not used, the\n"
"      output filename will be the same as the input\n"
"      file, with the `.pdf` file extension. When `--mode-multi` is used, this is\n"
"      the output directory. If `--output` is not used, the files are exported\n"
"      to the current directory.\n"
"| `-l <layer list>`, `--layers <layer list>`\n"
"    | A comma-separated list of layer names to export from the board, such as\n"
"      `F.Cu,B.Cu`. At least one layer must be given. Layer names can be\n"
"      specified as canonical layer names (`F.Cu`, `In.1`, `F.Fab`, etc.) or as\n"
"      user-defined (custom) layer names, but user-defined layer names are matched\n"
"      first.\n"
"| `--drawing-sheet <sheet path>`\n"
"    | Path to drawing sheet to use in plot, overriding the drawing sheet\n"
"      specified in the board file.\n"
"| `-D <variable name>=<value>`, `--define-var <variable_name>=<value>`\n"
"    | Add or override project variable definitions. Can be used multiple times\n"
"      to define multiple variables.\n"
"| `--subtract-soldermask`\n"
"    | Remove silkscreen from areas without soldermask.\n"
"| `-m`, `--mirror`\n"
"    | Mirror the board. This can be useful for showing bottom layers.\n"
"| `-t <theme name>`, `--theme <theme name>`\n"
"    | The name of the theme to use for export. If no theme is given, the\n"
"      board editor's currently selected theme is used.\n"
"| `-n`, `--negative`\n"
"    | Plot in negative.\n"
"| `--black-and-white`\n"
"    | Plot in black and white.\n"
"| `--sp`, `--sketch-pads-on-fab-layers`\n"
"    | Draw pad outlines and their numbers on front and back fab layers.\n"
"| `--hdnp`, `--hide-DNP-footprints-on-fab-layers`\n"
"    | Don't plot text and graphics of DNP footprints on fab layers.\n"
"| `--sdnp`, `--sketch-DNP-footprints-on-fab-layers`\n"
"    | Plot graphics of DNP footprints in sketch mode on fab layers.\n"
"| `--cdnp`, `--crossout-DNP-footprints-on-fab-layers`\n"
"    | Plot an \"X\" over the courtyard of DNP footprints on fab layers, and strikeout their reference designators.\n"
"| `--page-size-mode <mode>`\n"
"    | Set page sizing mode. Options are `0` (default), `1`, or `2`. `0` sets the\n"
"      output page size to fit the entire sheet, including drawing sheet frame\n"
"      and title block. `1` sets the output page size to match the current page\n"
"      size. `2` sets the output page size to the size of the board itself.\n"
"| `--fit-page-to-board`\n"
"    | Set the SVG size to match the board outline. This is equivalent to `--page-size-mode 2`.\n"
"| `--exclude-drawing-sheet`\n"
"    | Plot SVG without a drawing sheet.\n"
"| `--drill-shape-opt`\n"
"    | The shape of drill marks in the plot. Options are `0` for no drill marks,\n"
"      `1` for small marks, or `2` for actual size marks (default).\n"
"| `--cl <layer list>`, `--common-layers <layer list>`\n"
"    | A comma-separated list of layer names to plot on all layers, such as\n"
"      `F.Cu,B.Cu`. Layer names can be specified as canonical layer names\n"
"      (`F.Cu`, `In.1`, `F.Fab`, etc.) or as user-defined (custom) layer names,\n"
"      but user-defined layer names are matched first.\n"
"| `--mode-single`\n"
"    | Generates a single file with the output arg path acting as the complete directory and filename path. `COMMON_LAYER_LIST` does not function in this mode. Instead `LAYER_LIST` controls all layers plotted.\n"
"| `--mode-multi`\n"
"    | Plot the layers to one or more SVG files, with each file representing a\n"
"      single layer from `LAYER_LIST`. The output path specifies the directory in\n"
"      which the files will be written.\n"
"| `--plot-invisible-text`\n"
"    | Force plotting of values and references, even if they are invisible. This argument is deprecated as of KiCad\n"
"      9.0.1 and has no effect. It will be removed in a future version of KiCad. To plot invisible text, edit the\n"
"      board so that the text is no longer invisible.\n"
"| `--scale <scale>`\n"
"    | A scaling factor to use for plotting the PCB. The border and title block\n"
"      are not scaled. A scale factor of 0 autoscales the plot.\n"
"| `--check-zones`\n"
"    | Check zone fills and refill zones, if required, prior to export.\n"
"      Any zone fill updates are not saved in the board file.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: cli.adoc:1757
#, no-wrap
msgid "PCB VRML export"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:1760
msgid ""
"The `pcb export vrml` command exports a board design to a VRML 3D model file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:1762
msgid ""
"Usage: `kicad-cli pcb export vrml [--help] [--output OUTPUT_FILE] [--define-"
"var KEY=VALUE] [--force] [--no-unspecified] [--no-dnp] [--user-origin VAR] "
"[--units VAR] [--models-dir VAR] [--models-relative] INPUT_FILE`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: cli.adoc:1801
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `-h`, `--help`\n"
"    | Show help for the VRML export command.\n"
"| `-o <output filename>`, `--output <output filename>`\n"
"    | The output filename. When `--output` is not used, the output filename\n"
"      will be the same as the input file, with the `.wrl` file extension.\n"
"| `-D <variable name>=<value>`, `--define-var <variable_name>=<value>`\n"
"    | Add or override project variable definitions. Can be used multiple times\n"
"      to define multiple variables.\n"
"| `-f`, `--force`\n"
"    | Overwrite output file.\n"
"| `--no-unspecified`\n"
"    | Exclude 3D models of components with \"unspecified\" footprint type.\n"
"| `--no-dnp`\n"
"    | Exclude 3D models of components with \"Do not populate\" attribute.\n"
"| `--user-origin <output origin>`\n"
"    | Specify a custom origin for the output file, with X and Y coordinates. For\n"
"      example, `1x1in`, `1x1inch`, or `25.4x25.4mm`. The default unit is\n"
"      millimeters. If this option is not given, the board center is used.\n"
"| `--units <units>`\n"
"    | Units to use in the output file. Options are `mm`, `m`, `in` (default), or\n"
"      `tenths` (tenths of an inch).\n"
"| `--models-dir <output model directory>`\n"
"    | Name of output directory to copy component models into. If not used,\n"
"      component models are embedded into the output file.\n"
"| `--models-relative`\n"
"    | With `--models-dir`, use relative paths in the output file.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: cli.adoc:1803
#, no-wrap
msgid "PCB XAO export"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:1807
msgid ""
"The `pcb export xao` command exports a board design to an XAO (SALOME/Gmsh) "
"3D model file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:1809
msgid ""
"Usage: `kicad-cli pcb export xao [--help] [--output OUTPUT_FILE] [--define-"
"var KEY=VALUE] [--force] [--no-unspecified] [--no-dnp] [--grid-origin] [--"
"drill-origin] [--subst-models] [--board-only] [--cut-vias-in-body] [--no-"
"board-body] [--no-components] [--component-filter VAR] [--include-tracks] [--"
"include-pads] [--include-zones] [--include-inner-copper] [--include-"
"silkscreen] [--include-soldermask] [--fuse-shapes] [--fill-all-vias] [--min-"
"distance MIN_DIST] [--net-filter VAR] [--user-origin VAR] INPUT_FILE`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: cli.adoc:1880
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `-h`, `--help`\n"
"    | Show help for the XAO export command.\n"
"| `-o <output filename>`, `--output <output filename>`\n"
"    | The output filename. When `--output` is not used, the output filename\n"
"      will be the same as the input file, with the `.xao` file extension.\n"
"| `-D <variable name>=<value>`, `--define-var <variable_name>=<value>`\n"
"    | Add or override project variable definitions. Can be used multiple times\n"
"      to define multiple variables.\n"
"| `-f`, `--force`\n"
"    | Overwrite output file.\n"
"| `--no-unspecified`\n"
"    | Exclude 3D models of components with \"unspecified\" footprint type.\n"
"| `--no-dnp`\n"
"    | Exclude 3D models of components with \"Do not populate\" attribute.\n"
"| `--grid-origin`\n"
"    | Use grid origin as origin of output file.\n"
"| `--drill-origin`\n"
"    | Use drill origin as origin of output file.\n"
"| `--subst-models`\n"
"    | Replace VRML models in footprints with STEP or IGS models of the same\n"
"      name, if they exist.\n"
"| `--board-only`\n"
"    | Only include the board itself in the generated model; exclude all\n"
"      component models.\n"
"| `--cut-vias-in-body`\n"
"    | Cut via holes in board body even if conductor layers are not exported.\n"
"| `--no-board-body`\n"
"    | Exclude board body.\n"
"| `--no-components`\n"
"    | Exclude 3D models for components.\n"
"| `--component-filter <reference designator list>`\n"
"    | Only include component 3D models matching this list of reference\n"
"      designators (comma-separated, wildcards supported)\n"
"| `--include-tracks`\n"
"    | Include tracks and vias on outer conductor layers in export (time consuming).\n"
"| `--include-pads`\n"
"    | Include pads in export (time consuming).\n"
"| `--include-zones`\n"
"    | Include zones in export (time consuming).\n"
"| `--include-inner-copper`\n"
"    | Include elements on inner conductor layers in export.\n"
"| `--include-silkscreen`\n"
"    | Include silkscreen graphics in export as a set of flat faces.\n"
"| `--include-soldermask`\n"
"    | Include solder mask layers in export as a set of flat faces.\n"
"| `--fuse-shapes`\n"
"    | Fuse overlapping geometry together in export (time consuming).\n"
"| `--fill-all-vias`\n"
"    | Don't cut via holes in conductor layers.\n"
"| `--min-distance <min distance>`\n"
"    | Tolerance for considering two points to be in the same location. Default:\n"
"      `0.01mm`.\n"
"| `--net-filter <net filter>`\n"
"    | Only include copper items belonging to nets matching this wildcard.\n"
"| `--user-origin <output origin>`\n"
"    | Specify a custom origin for the output file, with X and Y coordinates. For\n"
"      example, `1x1in`, `1x1inch`, or `25.4x25.4mm`. The default unit is\n"
"      millimeters.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: cli.adoc:1882
#, no-wrap
msgid "PCB render"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:1885
msgid ""
"The `pcb render` command generates a raytraced rendering of the 3D model of "
"the board and saves it to a PNG or JPEG file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:1887
msgid ""
"Usage: `kicad-cli pcb render [--help] [--output OUTPUT_FILE] [--define-var "
"KEY=VALUE] [--width WIDTH] [--height HEIGHT] [--side SIDE] [--background BG] "
"[--quality QUALITY] [--preset PRESET] [--floor] [--perspective] [--zoom "
"ZOOM] [--pan VECTOR] [--pivot PIVOT] [--rotate ANGLES] [--light-top COLOR] "
"[--light-bottom COLOR] [--light-side COLOR] [--light-camera COLOR] [--light-"
"side-elevation ANGLE] INPUT_FILE`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: cli.adoc:1894
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `INPUT_FILE`\n"
"    | Board file to render.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: cli.adoc:1950
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `-h`, `--help`\n"
"    | Show help for the render command.\n"
"| `-o <output filename>`, `--output <output filename>`\n"
"    | The output filename. This argument must be given. The file extension given\n"
"      in this argument determines the output image file format. The filename\n"
"      must end with either `.png` (for PNG files) or `.jpg`/`.jpeg` (for JPG\n"
"      files).\n"
"| `-D <variable name>=<value>`, `--define-var <variable_name>=<value>`\n"
"    | Add or override project variable definitions. Can be used multiple times\n"
"      to define multiple variables.\n"
"| `-w <width>`, `--width <width>`\n"
"    | Image width in pixels. Default: `1600`.\n"
"| `-h <height>`, `--height <height>`\n"
"    | Image height in pixels. Default: `900`.\n"
"| `--side <side>`\n"
"    | The side of the board to render. Options are `top` (default), `bottom`, `left`, `right`, `front`, or `back`.\n"
"| `--background <background>`\n"
"    | Image background. Options are `default` (default), `transparent`, or\n"
"      `opaque`. For PNG files, `default` is `transparent`. For JPG files,\n"
"      `default` is `opaque`.\n"
"| `--quality <quality>`\n"
"    | Render quality. Options are `basic` (default), `high`, `user`. When `user`\n"
"      is specified, the render settings stored in the project are used.\n"
"| `--preset <color preset>`\n"
"    | Color preset. Options are `follow_pcb_editor`, `follow_plot_settings`\n"
"      (default), or `legacy_preset_flag`.\n"
"| `--floor`\n"
"    | Enables floor, shadows and post-processing, even if disabled in quality preset.\n"
"| `--perspective`\n"
"    | Use perspective projection instead of orthogonal.\n"
"| `--zoom <zoom level>`\n"
"    | Camera zoom factor as an integer. Default: `1`.\n"
"| `--pan <camera pan>`\n"
"    | Set camera pan location, in millimeters, with the format `'X,Y,Z'`, e.g. `'3,0,0'`.\n"
"| `--pivot <pivot>`\n"
"    | Set pivot point relative to the board center in centimeters, with the\n"
"      format `'X,Y,Z'` e.g. `'-10,2,0'`.\n"
"| `--rotate <rotation>`\n"
"    | Set board rotation around pivot point, in degrees, with the format\n"
"      `'X,Y,Z'`, e.g. `'-45,0,45'` for isometric view.\n"
"| `--light-top <intensity>`\n"
"    | Top light intensity, format `'R,G,B'` or a single number, range: 0-1.\n"
"| `--light-bottom <intensity>`\n"
"    | Bottom light intensity, format `'R,G,B'` or a single number, range: 0-1.\n"
"| `--light-side <intensity>`\n"
"    | Side lights intensity, format `'R,G,B'` or a single number, range: 0-1.\n"
"| `--light-camera <intensity>`\n"
"    | Camera light intensity, format `'R,G,B'` or a single number, range: 0-1.\n"
"| `--light-side-elevation <elevation>`\n"
"    | Side lights elevation angle in degrees, range: 0-90.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: cli.adoc:1952
#, no-wrap
msgid "PCB upgrade"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:1956
msgid ""
"The `pcb upgrade` command converts a KiCad board file from a previous KiCad "
"board file format to the native format for the current version of KiCad.  If "
"the input board file is already in the current file format, no action is "
"taken."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:1958
msgid "Usage: `kicad-cli pcb upgrade [--help] [--force] INPUT_FILE`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: cli.adoc:1965
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `INPUT_FILE`\n"
"    | Board file to upgrade.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: cli.adoc:1975
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `-h`, `--help`\n"
"    | Show help for the upgrade command.\n"
"| `--force`\n"
"    | Re-save the input board file even if it is already in the current file format.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: cli.adoc:1977
#, no-wrap
msgid "Schematic commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:1982
msgid ""
"The `sch` command runs an electrical rule check, exports a schematic to "
"various other file formats, or exports a bill of materials or netlist. Each "
"subcommand has its own options."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: cli.adoc:1983
#, no-wrap
msgid "Schematic ERC"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:1987
msgid ""
"The `sch erc` command runs an electrical rule check on a schematic and "
"generates a report."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:1989
msgid ""
"Usage: `kicad-cli sch erc [--help] [--output OUTPUT_FILE] [--define-var "
"KEY=VALUE] [--format VAR] [--units VAR] [--severity-all] [--severity-error] "
"[--severity-warning] [--severity-exclusions] [--exit-code-violations] "
"INPUT_FILE`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: cli.adoc:1996
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `INPUT_FILE`\n"
"    | Schematic file to run ERC on.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: cli.adoc:2031
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `-h`, `--help`\n"
"    | Show help for the ERC command.\n"
"| `-o <output filename>, `--output <output filename>`\n"
"    | Output filename for the generated ERC report. When `--output` is not\n"
"      used, the output filename will be the same as the input file, with the\n"
"      `.rpt` or `.json` file extension, depending on the selected format.\n"
"| `-D <variable name>=<value>`, `--define-var <variable_name>=<value>`\n"
"    | Add or override project variable definitions. Can be used multiple times\n"
"      to define multiple variables.\n"
"| `--format <format>`\n"
"    | Report file format. Options are `report` (default) or `json`.\n"
"| `--units <unit>`\n"
"    | Units to use in the report. Options are `mm` (default), `in`, or `mils`.\n"
"| `--severity-all`\n"
"    | Report all ERC violations. This is equivalent to using all of the other\n"
"      ERC severity options.\n"
"| `--severity-error`\n"
"    | Report all error-level ERC violations. This can be combined with the other\n"
"      ERC severity options.\n"
"| `--severity-warning`\n"
"    | Report all warning-level ERC violations. This can be combined with the\n"
"      other ERC severity options.\n"
"| `--severity-exclusions`\n"
"    | Report all excluded ERC violations. This can be combined with the other\n"
"      ERC severity options.\n"
"| `--exit-code-violations`\n"
"    | Return an exit code depending on whether or not ERC violations exist. The\n"
"      exit code is 0 if no violations are found, and 5 if any violations are\n"
"      found.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: cli.adoc:2033
#, no-wrap
msgid "Schematic bill of materials export"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2040
msgid ""
"The `sch export bom` command exports a BOM from a schematic.  The BOM export "
"has a number of options for controlling the format and included fields. This "
"export method is equivalent to xref:../eeschema/eeschema.adoc#bom-"
"export[exporting a BOM] from the symbol fields table."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2043
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To export a BOM using the legacy XML and Python BOM script workflow, use\n"
"      the `sch export python-bom` command.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2045
msgid ""
"Usage: `kicad-cli sch export bom [--help] [--output OUTPUT_FILE] [--preset "
"PRESET] [--format-preset FMT_PRESET] [--fields FIELDS] [--labels LABELS] [--"
"group-by GROUP_BY] [--sort-field SORT_BY] [--sort-asc] [--filter FILTER] [--"
"exclude-dnp] [--include-excluded-from-bom] [--field-delimiter FIELD_DELIM] "
"[--string-delimiter STR_DELIM] [--ref-delimiter REF_DELIM] [--ref-range-"
"delimiter REF_RANGE_DELIM] [--keep-tabs] [--keep-line-breaks] INPUT_FILE`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: cli.adoc:2052 cli.adoc:2117 cli.adoc:2164 cli.adoc:2193 cli.adoc:2297
#: cli.adoc:2324
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `INPUT_FILE`\n"
"    | Schematic file to export.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: cli.adoc:2102
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `-h`, `--help`\n"
"    | Shows help message and exits\n"
"| `-o <output filename>`, `--output <output filename>`\n"
"    | The output filename. When `--output` is not used, the output filename\n"
"      will be the same as the input file, with a `.csv` file extension.\n"
"| `--preset <preset>`\n"
"    | Use a named BOM preset setting from the schematic, e.g. `\"Grouped By Value\"`.\n"
"| `--format-preset <format preset>`\n"
"    | Use a named BOM format preset setting from the schematic, e.g. `CSV`.\n"
"| `--fields <fields>`\n"
"    | An ordered list of fields to export. `*` includes all fields. Special\n"
"      symbol fields such as DNP or Exclude from board can be accessed with\n"
"      `${DNP}` or `${EXCLUDE_FROM_BOARD}`, respectively (see the\n"
"      xref:../eeschema/eeschema.adoc#text-variables[text variable documentation]\n"
"      for a list of fields). Default: \"Reference,Value,Footprint,${QUANTITY},${DNP}\".\n"
"| `--labels <labels>`\n"
"    | An ordered list of labels to apply the exported fields (default:\n"
"      `\"Refs,Value,Footprint,Qty,DNP\"`).\n"
"| `--group-by <fields>`\n"
"    | Fields to group references by when field values match.\n"
"| `--sort-field <fields>`\n"
"    | Field name to sort by (default: `\"Reference\"`).\n"
"| `--sort-asc`\n"
"    | If given, sort in ascending order. If not given, sort in descending order.\n"
"| `--filter <filter>`\n"
"    | Filter string to remove output lines.\n"
"| `--exclude-dnp`\n"
"    | Exclude symbols with the \"Do not populate\" attribute.\n"
"| `--include-excluded-from-bom`\n"
"    | Include symbols marked \"Exclude from BOM\".\n"
"      This argument is deprecated as of KiCad 10.0 and has no effect. \n"
"| `--field-delimiter <delimiter>`\n"
"    | Separator between output fields/columns (default: `\",\"`).\n"
"| `--string-delimiter <delimiter>`\n"
"    | Character to surround fields with (none by default).\n"
"| `--ref-delimiter <delimiter>`\n"
"    | Character to place between individual references (default: `\",\"`).\n"
"| `--ref-range-delimiter <delimiter>`\n"
"    | Character to place in ranges of references (default: `\"-\"`). Leave blank for\n"
"      no ranges.\n"
"| `--keep-tabs`\n"
"    | Keep tab characters from input fields. Stripped by default.\n"
"| `--keep-line-breaks`\n"
"    | Keep line break characters from input fields. Stripped by default.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: cli.adoc:2104
#, no-wrap
msgid "Schematic DXF export"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2108
msgid ""
"The `sch export dxf` command exports a schematic to a DXF file. Each sheet "
"in the design is exported to its own file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2110
msgid ""
"Usage: `kicad-cli sch export dxf [--help] [--output OUTPUT_DIR] [--drawing-"
"sheet SHEET_PATH] [--define-var KEY=VALUE] [--theme THEME_NAME] [--black-and-"
"white] [--exclude-drawing-sheet] [--default-font VAR] [--pages PAGE_LIST] "
"INPUT_FILE`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: cli.adoc:2148
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `-h`, `--help`\n"
"    | Show help for the DXF file export command.\n"
"| `-o <output dir>`, `--output <output dir>`\n"
"    | The output folder for the exported files. One file is output for each\n"
"      sheet. When `--output` is not used, the files are exported to the\n"
"      current directory.\n"
"| `--drawing-sheet <sheet path>`\n"
"    | Path to drawing sheet to use in plot, overriding the drawing sheet\n"
"      specified in the schematic file.\n"
"| `-D <variable name>=<value>`, `--define-var <variable_name>=<value>`\n"
"    | Add or override project variable definitions. Can be used multiple times\n"
"      to define multiple variables.\n"
"| `-t <theme name>`, `--theme <theme name>`\n"
"    | The name of the theme to use for export. If no theme is given, the\n"
"      schematic editor's currently selected theme is used.\n"
"| `-b`, `--black-and-white`\n"
"    | Export schematic in black and white.\n"
"| `-e`, `--exclude-drawing-sheet`\n"
"    | Plot DXF without a drawing sheet.\n"
"| `--default-font <font name>`\n"
"    | Default font name. Default: `\"KiCad Font\"`.\n"
"| `-p <page list>`, `--pages <page list>`\n"
"    | Comma-separated list of pages to export. Blank or unspecified means all\n"
"      pages. To plot specific pages, give the root sheet as `INPUT_FILE` and\n"
"      specify the desired output pages with the `--pages` argument.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: cli.adoc:2150
#, no-wrap
msgid "Schematic netlist export"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2155
msgid ""
"The `sch export netlist` command exports a netlist in xref:../eeschema/"
"eeschema.adoc#netlist-formats[various formats] from a schematic."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2157
msgid ""
"Usage: `kicad-cli sch export netlist [--help] [--output OUTPUT_FILE] [--"
"format FORMAT] INPUT_FILE`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: cli.adoc:2178
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `-h`, `--help`\n"
"    | Show help for the netlist export command.\n"
"| `-o <output filename>`, `--output <output filename>`\n"
"    | The output filename. When `--output` is not used, the output filename\n"
"      will be the same as the input file, with a `.net` file extension.\n"
"| `-f <format>`, `--format <format>`\n"
"    | The netlist output format. Options are `kicadsexpr` (default), `kicadxml`,\n"
"      `cadstar`, `orcadpcb2`, `spice`, `spicemodel`, `pads`, or `allegro`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: cli.adoc:2180
#, no-wrap
msgid "Schematic PDF export"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2184
msgid ""
"The `sch export pdf` command exports a schematic to a PDF file. Each sheet "
"in the design is exported to its own page in the PDF file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2186
msgid ""
"Usage: `kicad-cli sch export pdf [--help] [--output OUTPUT_FILE] [--drawing-"
"sheet SHEET_PATH] [--define-var KEY=VALUE] [--theme THEME_NAME] [--black-and-"
"white] [--exclude-drawing-sheet] [--default-font VAR] [--exclude-pdf-"
"property-popups] [--exclude-pdf-hierarchical-links] [--exclude-pdf-metadata] "
"[--no-background-color] [--pages PAGE_LIST] INPUT_FILE`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: cli.adoc:2231
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `-h`, `--help`\n"
"    | Show help for the PDF file export command.\n"
"| `-o <output filename>`, `--output <output filename>`\n"
"    | The output filename. When `--output` is not used, the output filename\n"
"      will be the same as the input file, with a `.pdf` file extension.\n"
"| `--drawing-sheet <sheet path>`\n"
"    | Path to drawing sheet to use in plot, overriding the drawing sheet\n"
"      specified in the schematic file.\n"
"| `-D <variable name>=<value>`, `--define-var <variable_name>=<value>`\n"
"    | Add or override project variable definitions. Can be used multiple times\n"
"      to define multiple variables.\n"
"| `-t <theme name>`, `--theme <theme name>`\n"
"    | The name of the theme to use for export. If no theme is given, the\n"
"      schematic editor's currently selected theme is used.\n"
"| `-b`, `--black-and-white`\n"
"    | Export schematic in black and white.\n"
"| `-e`, `--exclude-drawing-sheet`\n"
"    | Plot PDF without a drawing sheet.\n"
"| `--default-font <font name>`\n"
"    | Default font name. Default: `\"KiCad Font\"`.\n"
"| `--exclude-pdf-property-popups`\n"
"    | Do not generate property popups in PDF.\n"
"| `--exclude-pdf-hierarchical-links`\n"
"    | Do not generate clickable links for hierarchical elements in PDF.\n"
"| `--exclude-pdf-metadata`\n"
"    | Do not generate PDF metadata from AUTHOR and SUBJECT variables.\n"
"| `-n`, `--no-background-color`\n"
"    | Export schematic without a background color, regardless of theme.\n"
"| `-p <page list>`, `--pages <page list>`\n"
"    | Comma-separated list of pages to export. Blank or unspecified means all\n"
"      pages. To plot specific pages, give the root sheet as `INPUT_FILE` and\n"
"      specify the desired output pages with the `--pages` argument.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: cli.adoc:2233
#, no-wrap
msgid "Schematic PostScript export"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2237
msgid ""
"The `sch export ps` command exports a schematic to a PostScript file. Each "
"sheet in the design is exported to its own file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2239
msgid ""
"Usage: `kicad-cli sch export ps [--help] [--output OUTPUT_DIR] [--drawing-"
"sheet SHEET_PATH] [--define-var KEY=VALUE] [--theme THEME_NAME] [--black-and-"
"white] [--exclude-drawing-sheet] [--default-font VAR] [--no-background-"
"color] [--pages PAGE_LIST] INPUT_FILE`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: cli.adoc:2246
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `INPUT_DIR`\n"
"    | Schematic file to export.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: cli.adoc:2279
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `-h`, `--help`\n"
"    | Show help for the PS file export command.\n"
"| `-o <output dir>`, `--output <output dir>`\n"
"    | The output folder for the exported files. One file is output for each\n"
"      sheet. When `--output` is not used, the files are exported to the\n"
"      current directory.\n"
"| `--drawing-sheet <sheet path>`\n"
"    | Path to drawing sheet to use in plot, overriding the drawing sheet\n"
"      specified in the schematic file.\n"
"| `-D <variable name>=<value>`, `--define-var <variable_name>=<value>`\n"
"    | Add or override project variable definitions. Can be used multiple times\n"
"      to define multiple variables.\n"
"| `-t <theme name>`, `--theme <theme name>`\n"
"    | The name of the theme to use for export. If no theme is given, the\n"
"      schematic editor's currently selected theme is used.\n"
"| `-b`, `--black-and-white`\n"
"    | Export schematic in black and white.\n"
"| `-e`, `--exclude-drawing-sheet`\n"
"    | Plot PS without a drawing sheet.\n"
"| `--default-font <font name>`\n"
"    | Default font name. Default: `\"KiCad Font\"`.\n"
"| `-n`, `--no-background-color`\n"
"    | Export schematic without a background color, regardless of theme.\n"
"| `-p <page list>`, `--pages <page list>`\n"
"    | Comma-separated list of pages to export. Blank or unspecified means all\n"
"      pages. To plot specific pages, give the root sheet as `INPUT_FILE` and\n"
"      specify the desired output pages with the `--pages` argument.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: cli.adoc:2281
#, no-wrap
msgid "Schematic bill of materials export (legacy BOM scripts)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2288
msgid ""
"The `sch export python-bom` command exports an XML BOM file from a "
"schematic.  The XML BOM file can then be processed into your desired BOM "
"format using a custom script or one of the scripts described in the xref:../"
"eeschema/eeschema.adoc#bom-export[schematic BOM export documentation]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2290
msgid ""
"Usage: `kicad-cli sch export python-bom [--help] [--output OUTPUT_FILE] "
"INPUT_FILE`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: cli.adoc:2309
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `-h`, `--help`\n"
"    | Show help for the BOM export command.\n"
"| `-o <output filename>`, `--output <output filename>`\n"
"    | The output filename. When `--output` is not used, the output filename\n"
"      will be the same as the input file, with a `-bom.xml` suffix and file\n"
"      extension.\n"
msgstr ""

