#. type: Title ===
#: cli.adoc:2358
#, no-wrap
msgid "Schematic upgrade"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2362
msgid ""
"The `sch upgrade` command converts a KiCad schematic file from a previous "
"KiCad schematic file format to the native format for the current version of "
"KiCad.  If the input schematic file is already in the current file format, "
"no action is taken."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2365
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Only the specified schematic file is upgraded.\n"
"      If the schematic file contains any child sheets, the child sheets are not upgraded.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2367
msgid "Usage: `kicad-cli sch upgrade [--help] [--force] INPUT_FILE`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: cli.adoc:2374
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `INPUT_FILE`\n"
"    | Schematic file to upgrade.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: cli.adoc:2384
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `-h`, `--help`\n"
"    | Show help for the upgrade command.\n"
"| `--force`\n"
"    | Re-save the input schematic file even if it is already in the current file format.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: cli.adoc:2386
#, no-wrap
msgid "Symbol commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2390
msgid ""
"The `sym` subcommand exports symbols to another format or upgrades symbol "
"libraries to the current version of the KiCad symbol file format."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: cli.adoc:2391
#, no-wrap
msgid "Symbol export"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2395
msgid ""
"The `sym export svg` command exports one or more symbols from the specified "
"library into SVG files."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2397
msgid ""
"Usage: `kicad-cli sym export svg [--help] [--output OUTPUT_DIR] [--theme "
"THEME_NAME] [--symbol SYMBOL] [--black-and-white] [--include-hidden-pins] [--"
"include-hidden-fields] INPUT_FILE`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: cli.adoc:2404
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `INPUT_FILE`\n"
"    | Symbol library file to use for export.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: cli.adoc:2428
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `-h`, `--help`\n"
"    | Show help for the symbol SVG export command.\n"
"| `-o <output dir>`, `--output <output dir>`\n"
"    | The output folder for the exported files. Each symbol in the input library\n"
"      is output to a separate file. When `--output` is not used, the files\n"
"      are exported to the current directory.\n"
"| `-t <theme name>`, `--theme <theme name>`\n"
"    | The name of the theme to use for export. If no theme is given, the symbol\n"
"      editor's currently selected theme is used.\n"
"| `-s <symbol name>`, `--symbol <symbol name>`\n"
"    | The specific symbol to export from the library. When this argument is\n"
"      not used, all symbols in the library are exported.\n"
"| `--black-and-white`\n"
"    | Export symbols in black and white.\n"
"| `--include-hidden-pins`\n"
"    | Export hidden pins in the exported SVG.\n"
"| `--include-hidden-fields`\n"
"    | Export hidden symbol fields in the exported SVG.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: cli.adoc:2430
#, no-wrap
msgid "Symbol upgrade"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2436
msgid ""
"The `sym upgrade` command converts the specified symbol library from a "
"legacy KiCad symbol format or a non-KiCad symbol format to the native format "
"for the current version of KiCad. If the input library is already in the "
"current file format, no action is taken."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2438
msgid "Supported input symbol formats are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2440
msgid "KiCad symbol library (`.kicad_sym`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2441
msgid "KiCad (pre-6.0) symbol library (`.lib`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2442
msgid "Altium schematic library (`.SchLib`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2444
msgid "CADSTAR parts library (`.lib`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2449
msgid ""
"Usage: `kicad-cli sym upgrade [--help] [--output OUTPUT_FILE] [--force] "
"INPUT_FILE`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: cli.adoc:2456
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `INPUT_FILE`\n"
"    | Symbol library to upgrade.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: cli.adoc:2469
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `-h`, `--help`\n"
"    | Show help for the upgrade command.\n"
"| `-o <output filename>`, `--output <output filename>`\n"
"    | The output filename for the upgraded symbol library. When `--output` is\n"
"      not used, the upgraded symbol library is saved over the original library.\n"
"| `--force`\n"
"    | Re-save the input library even if it is already in the current file format.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: cli.adoc:2471
#, no-wrap
msgid "Version commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2476
msgid ""
"The `version` command prints the KiCad version. Without any arguments, it "
"simply prints the version number, for example `7.0.7`. You can print the "
"version in several other formats using the `--format` argument."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2479
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use `kicad-cli version --format about` for version information to include\n"
"      when submitting bug reports or feature requests on Gitlab.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: cli.adoc:2481
msgid "Usage: `kicad-cli version [--help] [--format VAR]`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: cli.adoc:2493
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `--format <format>`\n"
"    | Format of the version number. Options are `plain` (default), `commit`, or\n"
"      `about`. `plain` prints the version number (e.g. `7.0.7`), which is the\n"
"      default if the `--format` argument is not used. `commit` prints the hash\n"
"      of the git commit for the build of KiCad you are using. `about` prints the\n"
"      full version information, including library versions and basic system\n"
"      information. You can use the `about` version information in bug reports.\n"
msgstr ""
